/**
 * The English string table — and, because it is `as const`, the SCHEMA.
 *
 * `StringKey` is `keyof typeof EN` (see `table.ts`), so this file decides which
 * keys exist. Add a key here and every other language fails to typecheck until
 * it has one too; that is the mechanism that keeps a Dutch screen from showing
 * an English sentence.
 *
 * English is also the fallback: `t()` reaches for this table when a key is
 * missing elsewhere, and `DEFAULT_TRANSLATE` is bound to it. So a value here is
 * never allowed to be a placeholder or a TODO — it is what somebody will
 * actually read.
 */
